BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Time’s Second Arrow: Evolution\, Order\, and a New Law of Nature
DTSTART:20261103T000000
DTEND:20261103T000000
DTSTAMP:20261103T185444Z
UID:13bf8aa3bb4caf945dbaa256612a5a@events-near-me
DESCRIPTION:Stars\, planets\, minerals\, and living organisms can become i
 ncreasingly diverse and complex over vast spans of time. Yet no existing l
 aw of nature fully describes or predicts how these complex systems evolve.
  In this talk\, Robert Hazen will introduce a proposed new natural law tha
 t applies to nonliving\, living\, and symbolic systems. The law suggests t
 hat evolution is not limited to biology but occurs throughout the universe
 . It is based on the idea that systems made up of many interacting parts c
 an gradually develop new ways of functioning. Hazen describes this process
  as a possible “second arrow of time\,” working alongside the familiar
  tendency toward greater disorder described by thermodynamics. Join us to 
 learn how researchers are testing this idea by studying the evolution of m
 inerals\, soil microbes\, tumors\, languages\, and AI. Free event parking 
 is available with registration. Register by November 2 to receive parking 
 registration instructions. Presented by the Harvard Museum of Natural Hist
 ory and the Harvard Museums of Science & Culture. LEARN MORE / GET TICKETS
  Sources: Meet Boston Event page: https://www.meetboston.com/event/time%e2
 %80%99s-second-arrow%3a-evolution-order-and-a-new-law-of-nature/93902/\n\n
 Events Near Me: within 30 miles of Northborough\, MA 01532\nDiscovery: Loc
 al fallback from massachusetts-events.ics\nSource page: https://www.meetbo
 ston.com/event/time%e2%80%99s-second-arrow%3a-evolution-order-and-a-new-la
 w-of-nature/93902/
LOCATION:Geological Lecture Hall\, Geological Lecture Hall 24 Oxford Stree
 t\, Cambridge\, MA\, 02138
URL:https://www.meetboston.com/event/time%e2%80%99s-second-arrow%3a-evolut
 ion-order-and-a-new-law-of-nature/93902/
END:VEVENT
