 ors: Celeste Ng\, bestselling author of "Little Fires Everywhere"\; Annabe
 l Monaghan\, New York Times bestselling author of beloved contemporary nov
 els\; and Jennifer Givhan\, award-winning poet and novelist. The discussio
 n will be moderated by Stephanie Pasha\, president of the Worcester Public
  Library Board of Directors. The evening also includes delicious food from
  Simply Delicious Catering\, complimentary beer and wine\, and a signature
  drink\, all in support of the programs and services that make the Worcest
 er Public Library an essential resource for our community. We’ll also pr
 esent the 2026 Dr. Richard E. Greene Founders Award to Lisa Kirby Gibbs. T
 hursday\, November 5\, 2026 | 5:45–9 p.m. Worcester Public Library | 3 S
 alem Square\, Worcester Tickets: $175 per person Register now: https://lp.
