BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:ValleyCAST Presents: A Conversation with The Blackstone River | Op
 ening Reception
DTSTART:20261105T000000
DTEND:20261105T000000
DTSTAMP:20261103T185444Z
UID:3c34d135711e9adbe7cf33fb8aff75@events-near-me
DESCRIPTION:Spanning 50 miles from Worcester to Providence\, the Blackston
 e River features distinct contrasts - from urban and industrial centers to
  rural and natural environments\, shaped by both heavy industrial use and 
 ongoing conservation efforts. Through aerial and ground-level photography
 \, long-time Blackstone Valley photographers James Hunt and Bob Evans show
 case ecological history and diverse landscapes rarely seen by the casual o
 bserver. Opening reception with light refreshments: Thursday\, November 5
 \, 5–8 pm Gallery hours: Monday–Friday\, 9 am–4 pm On view through D
 ecember 18\, 2026 Incorporating both digital imagery and traditional film
 \, this exhibition brings together two complimentary artistic perspectives
 . James Hunt draws on a decade of environmental photography and his backgr
 ound in sustainability to piece together the River’s multi-layered story
 \, accompanied by the short film A Brief Conversation with the Blackstone 
 River (co-created with Evans). Bob Evans applies a meticulous\, engineerin
 g-informed eye to capture human impact\, quiet decay\, and structural deta
 ils along the waterway. Together\, their work invites viewers to look beyo
 nd the surface\, consider the River’s storied past\, and re-examine our 
 collective responsibility to the natural world. Sources: Discover Central 
 Massachusetts Event page: https://www.discovercentralma.org/event/valleyca
 st-presents%3a-a-conversation-with-the-blackstone-river-%7c-opening-recept
 ion/31166/\n\nEvents Near Me: within 30 miles of Northborough\, MA 01532\n
 Discovery: Local fallback from massachusetts-events.ics\nSource page: http
 s://www.discovercentralma.org/event/valleycast-presents%3a-a-conversation-
 with-the-blackstone-river-%7c-opening-reception/31166/
LOCATION:Heritage Gallery\, 50 Douglas Road\, Whitinsville\, MA\, 01588
URL:https://www.discovercentralma.org/event/valleycast-presents%3a-a-conve
 rsation-with-the-blackstone-river-%7c-opening-reception/31166/
END:VEVENT
