BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Asa Waters Mansion Presents: The American Lyceum Movement
DTSTART:20261107T000000
DTEND:20261108T000000
DTSTAMP:20261103T185444Z
UID:97bc848218a2ce0c1ceba6aacd7356@events-near-me
DESCRIPTION:Two hundred years ago a community-focused education movement b
 egan in Millbury\, Massachusetts and quickly spread to thousands of locati
 ons across the Northeast and Midwest United States. Neighbors came togethe
 r with good will to share knowledge\, socialize and strengthen community b
 onds. Welcome back to the American Lyceum movement. The Massachusetts Cent
 er for Civic Education and the historic Asa Waters Mansion\, both in Millb
 ury\, invite you to a weekend of events this November to learn about the h
 istory of this movement and its roots in Worcester County and take part in
  shaping its 21st century impact on our communities. Please join us on Sat
 urday\, November 7th\, and Sunday\, November 8th at Asa Waters Mansion\, l
 ocated at 123 Elm Street\, Millbury\, MA 01527. Five scheduled events will
  take place at the mansion throughout the weekend. Most are free. Guests a
 re invited to attend as many as they’d like. The keynote speaker for the
 se events will be Dr. Angela G. Ray\, a noted lyceum scholar at Northweste
 rn University and a published author on the American Lyceum Movement. Dr. 
 Ray will participate in each of the weekend’s programs. Josiah Holbrook
 \, a farmer and Yale graduate\, founded the first lyceum in Millbury in No
 vember 1826. The word “lyceum” is unique: it refers to the garden near
  the Temple of Apollo in ancient Greece where Aristotle dispensed knowledg
 e nearly 2\,500 years ago. Some communities retain their lyceums even toda
 y in dedicated spaces designed for that purpose - but a lyceum can take pl
 ace anywhere at any time. A lyceum can address any topic that will bring c
 ommunity members together to learn\, socialize in person and strengthen co
 mmunity ties. On Saturday\, November 7th\, three events will celebrate the
  history of this movement: • A mid-morning (10:00am – 12:00pm) interac
 tive brunch lecture will examine the history of the American lyceum moveme
 nt. This is a ticketed event with limited seating in the Great Room of the
  historic mansion. Tickets will be $35 per person. Please register online 
 through our secure UniBank Unipay site at https://unipaygold.unibank.com/t
 ransactionInfo.aspx?CustomerID=1686&TransID=39039. • A FREE afternoon in
 formative\, interactive program (2:00pm to 4:00pm) with refreshments is op
 en to the general public and will focus on the very local roots of this mo
 vement which quickly blossomed across the young nation. This event is FREE
  of charge\, but attendees should register to reserve their seats by calli
 ng Asa Waters Mansion Director\, Traci Parath\, at 508.865.0855 or email T
 raci at tparath@millburyma.gov. • An evening reenactment of the young Ab
 raham Lincoln’s famous lyceum speech will take place by candlelight (7:0
 0pm to 9:00pm) in this period-appropriate setting and feature an interacti
 ve multimedia presentation. This is a ticketed event with limited seating 
 in the Great Room of the historic mansion. Tickets will be $10 per person.
  Please register online through our secure UniBank Unipay site at https://
 unipaygold.unibank.com/transactionInfo.aspx?CustomerID=1686&TransID=39040.
  On Sunday\, November 8th\, two events will focus on what a lyceum in the 
 21st century can be: • A FREE mid-morning program (10:00am – 12:00pm) 
 will feature an interactive panel discussion about what the lyceum movemen
 t should look like today. Attendees will break into smaller groups to brai
 nstorm about topics that would draw friends and neighbors to a modern lyce
 um. These ideas will be documented and put into use as modern day lyceums 
 are designed and offered to the public in local communities. This event is
  FREE of charge\, but attendees should register to reserve their seats by 
 calling Asa Waters Mansion Director\, Traci Parath\, at 508.865.0855 or em
 ail Traci at tparath@millburyma.gov. • The FREE afternoon program (1:00p
 m to 3:00pm) attend an actual modern lyceum and learn something new. Choos
 e one of these two lively topics: o “A Life In Art” – Meet and talk 
 with Millbury’s three renowned artists. Michael Graves\, Scott Nelson an
 d Michael Wackell will display their work\, explain their techniques and d
 escribe the process of making a successful life through art. o “Perspect
 ives on AI” – Consider artificial intelligence (AI) from multiple pers
 pectives. Engage with State Senator Michael Moore (Second Worcester Distri
 ct) and others from a variety of sectors who are dealing with the impacts 
 of AI. This event is FREE of charge\, but attendees should register to res
 erve their seats by calling Asa Waters Mansion Director\, Traci Parath\, a
 t 508.865.0855 or email Traci at tparath@millburyma.gov. All events take p
 lace at the beautifully restored historic Asa Waters Mansion\, which is al
 so celebrating its 200th Anniversary in 2026. The mansion is located in do
 wntown Millbury\, itself easily accessible from Routes 90\, 290\, 190\, 14
 6 and 20. Free local parking is available. For more information\, please c
 ontact Asa Waters Mansion Executive Director\, Traci Parath at 508.865.085
 5 or email Traci at\, tparath@millburyma.gov. Sources: Discover Central Ma
 ssachusetts Event page: https://www.discovercentralma.org/event/asa-waters
 -mansion-presents%3a-the-american-lyceum-movement/31160/\n\nEvents Near Me
 : within 30 miles of Northborough\, MA 01532\nDiscovery: Local fallback fr
 om massachusetts-events.ics\nSource page: https://www.discovercentralma.or
 g/event/asa-waters-mansion-presents%3a-the-american-lyceum-movement/31160/
LOCATION:Asa Waters Mansion\, 123 Elm St.\, Millbury\, MA\, 01527
URL:https://www.discovercentralma.org/event/asa-waters-mansion-presents%3a
 -the-american-lyceum-movement/31160/
END:VEVENT
