DTEND:20261107T000000
DTSTAMP:20261103T185444Z
UID:f18c34f675804c0d886c67c1446241@events-near-me
DESCRIPTION:Meet up-and-coming scientists and learn about questions at the
  forefront of research today in this series of short talks. Speaker: Aleez
 ah Madraswalla\, Research Assistant at the Allard Lab at Harvard Medical S
 chool Have you ever wished you had a superpower? Some animals have already
  figured it out! Did you know that sea robins have evolved legs to walk al
 ong the seafloor? Or that some sea slugs can steal special abilities from 
 their prey? Join Harvard scientist Aleezah Madraswalla to discover how the
 se amazing adaptations help animals survive—and give them a leg up! Reco
 mmended for ages 10 and up. Regular museum admission rates apply. Presente
 d by the Harvard Museum of Natural History and Harvard Museums of Science 
 & Culture LEARN MORE / GET TICKETS Sources: Meet Boston Event page: https:
 //www.meetboston.com/event/walking-fish-and-photosynthesizing-sea-slugs/93
