BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Superheroes for cCMV Family Walk/Run/Roll
DTSTART:20261108T000000
DTEND:20261108T000000
DTSTAMP:20261103T185444Z
UID:7017dcaa5cbed9bd5384ffb5e26807@events-near-me
DESCRIPTION:Date: Sunday\, November 8th\, 2026 Location: The Learning Cent
 er for the Deaf (Framingham\, MA) Start Time: 10 AM Join us this November 
 at The Learning Center for the Deaf as we come together to raise funds for
  cCMV education and research. Enjoy a meaningful day surrounded by other f
 amilies and advocates who share a passion for making a difference in the c
 CMV community. Fees: $25/person $15/youth $75/family of 4 or more Children
  age 3 and under are free All registered children will receive a cape to d
 ecorate at the event! Course - This short walk/run/roll is is geared towar
 ds families and children and will be untimed. Participants will complete t
 wo laps around a soccer field at their own pace. Event Festivities: In add
 ition to the walk/run/roll\, there will be a bounce house\, face-painting
 \, a playground\, food trucks\, and other games & activities for families 
 to enjoy. Raffle: We will be raffling off baskets and more at the event! C
 ash or Pay Pal will be accepted. $1/ticket or $20 for 25 tickets. Accessib
 ility: ASL interpreters will be available throughout the event. This event
  will be accessible for all. Parking: There are several lots available aro
 und The Learning Center. Additional parking information will be shared wit
 h all registered participants. Pets: Only service animals are permitted on
  campus. Fundraising/donations: All funds raised (including registration f
 ees) will go to the Massachusetts Congenital CMV Coalition and the Nationa
 l CMV Foundation to help support them in their mission of promoting cCMV e
 ducation and awareness\, in order to lessen its incidence and improve outc
 omes. WHAT IS cCMV? Congenital Cytomegalovirus (cCMV) is the most common i
 nfectious cause of birth defects and the leading non-genetic cause of hear
 ing loss. 1 in 200 babies are born with the virus\, but only 9% of women k
 now about it or how to prevent it. WHERE CAN I FIND OUT MORE ABOUT CMV? cm
 vmass.org & nationalcmv.org Event Contact: info@cmvmass.org Sources: Disco
 ver Central Massachusetts Event page: https://www.discovercentralma.org/ev
